Confidence Level). Includes batch drift detection. |\n| **[modules/profitability.py](file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/neurax_app/modules/profitability.py)** | **Economic & What-If Engine**: Translates operational metrics into financial metrics (Scrap Material Loss, Bottleneck Idle Cost, Opportunity Loss, Net Margin) with interactive sliders and instant What-If profit uplift simulation. |\n| **[utils/chart_helpers.py](file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/neurax_app/utils/chart_helpers.py)** | **Plotly Visuals**: Financial waterfall chart, Multi-model radar chart, Station utilization bars, and defect drift line charts. |\n| **[README.md](file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/neurax_app/README.md)** | **Full Hackathon Documentation**: Covers problem understanding, system architecture diagrams, and approach for Checkpoint 1 (15 marks). |\n\n---\n\n### 💡 Hackathon Evaluation Coverage (100 Marks)\n- **Checkpoint 1 (15 Marks)**: The **[README.md](file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/neurax_app/README.md)** includes problem framing, Mermaid architecture diagrams, and mathematical formulations (TOC, Little's Law).\n- **Checkpoint 2 (25 Marks)**: Fully working execution integrating inspection images, 3 Rockwell Arena CSV models, and economic parameters.\n- **Checkpoint 3 (60 Marks)**: YOLOv8 defect detection + bounding boxes + UNCERTAIN/NOVEL guards + TOC bottleneck identification + evidence-based causal recommendations + what-if financial simulations.\n\nDetailed notes and instructions are documented in **[walkthrough.md](file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/brain/f365fb6f-b130-4162-803f-d8faca0d55a2/walkthrough.md)**."}
