d['cause']}</b>\n  <span class=\"badge badge-{conf}\" style=\"float:right\">{conf} CONFIDENCE</span><br>\n  <small>📏 <b>Evidence:</b> {card['evidence']}</small><br>\n  <small>🦠 <b>Related Defects:</b> {', '.join(card['related_defects']) if card['related_defects'] else 'General throughput issue'}\n  {'&nbsp; <span class=\"badge badge-DEFECT\">OBSERVED ✓</span>' if obs else ''}</small><br>\n  <hr style=\"margin:8px 0; border-color:#334\">\n  <small>✅ <b>Recommended Action:</b> {card['action']}</small>\n</div>\n\"\"\"\n                st.markdown(html, unsafe_allow_html=True)\n\n        st.divider()\n\n        # ── Drift analysis ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n        st.markdown(\"### 📈 Defect Rate Drift Analysis\")\n        if no_quality or len(registry) < 2:\n            st.info(\"Inspect at least 2 units to see drift trends.\")\n        else:\n            drift_df_raw = registry.drift_dataframe()\n            drift        = drift_analysis(drift_df_raw)\n\n            if drift:\n                dc1, dc2, dc3 = st.columns(3)\n                dc1.metric(\"Trend Direction\", drift['trend'])\n                dc2.metric(\"Slope\", f\"{drift['slope']:+.2f} pp/unit\")\n                dc3.metric(\"Units Needing Review\",\n                           drift['novel_count'] + drift['uncertain_count'])\n\n                st.plotly_chart(defect_trend(drift['df']), use_container_width=True)\n\n        # ── Novel / Uncertain summary ──────────────────────────────────────────\n        if not no_quality:\n            flagged = flag_novel(registry.to_dataframe())\n            if not flagged.empty:\n                st.warning(f\"### 🟣 {len(flagged)} Novel / Uncertain Unit(s) — Human Review Required\")\n                st.markdown(\n                    \"These units have confidence scores below the classification threshold. \"\n                    \"They may represent **new defect types** not seen during training.\"\n                )\n                st.datafram