{"step_index":106,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T14:39:06Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-19T20:09:06+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-19T20:09:07+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/neurax_app/modules/defect_detector.py`\nTotal Lines: 221\nTotal Bytes: 8405\nShowing lines 175 to 221\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n175: \n176: \n177: # ── Image Annotation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n178: \n179: def annotate_image(img: Image.Image, detections: list[dict], status: str) -> Image.Image:\n180:     \"\"\"Draw boxes, labels, and a status badge onto the image.\"\"\"\n181:     draw = ImageDraw.Draw(img, 'RGBA')\n182:     w, h = img.size\n183: \n184:     border_color = STATUS_COLORS.get(status, '#95a5a6')\n185: \n186:     # Status border\n187:     bw = 6\n188:     draw.rectangle([0, 0, w - 1, h - 1], outline=border_color, width=bw)\n189: \n190:     # Bounding boxes\n191:     for det in detections:\n192:         if det.get('bbox') is None:\n193:             continue\n194:         x1, y1, x2, y2 = [int(v) for v in det['bbox']]\n195:         color = DEFECT_COLORS.get(det['defect_type'].lower(), '#e74c3c')\n196:         draw.rectangle([x1, y1, x2, y2], outline=color, width=3)\n197: \n198:         label = f\"{det['defect_type'].upper()} {det['confidence']:.2f}\"\n199:         text_w = len(label) * 7\n200:         text_h = 18\n201:         draw.rectangle([x1, y1 - text_h - 2, x1 + text_w, y1], fill=color)\n202:         try:\n203:             font = ImageFont.truetype(\"arial.ttf\", 13)\n204:         except Exception:\n205:             font = ImageFont.load_default()\n206:         draw.text((x1 + 2, y1 - text_h), label, fill='white', font=font)\n207: \n208:     # Status badge (top-right)\n209:     badge_text = status\n210:     badge_color = STATUS_COLORS.get(status, '#95a5a6')\n211:     bx1, by1 = w - 110, 10\n212:     bx2, by2 = w - 10,  38\n213:     draw.rectangle([bx1, by1, bx2, by2], fill=badge_color)\n214:     try:\n215:         font_badge = ImageFont.truetype(\"arialbd.ttf\", 13)\n216:     except Exception:\n217:         font_badge = ImageFont.load_default()\n218:     draw.text((bx1 + 6, by1 + 4), badge_text, fill='white', font=font_badge)\n219: \n220:     return img\n221: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":107,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T14:39:14Z","thinking":"The existing code skips detections without bounding boxes, which is correct for classification models. However, drawing a border around the entire image frame creates a misleading \"framed\" appearance, failing to localize defects. The aim is to implement automated defect localization.\n\n\nConsidering how to localize defects, it's necessary to adapt the classification model's output to provide bounding box coordinates. Suspect OpenCV's image processing capabilities can identify visual signatures specific to each defect type. For cracks/scratches, this means gradient analysis; for holes, connected component detection; and for rust, color space analysis.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python -c \"import cv2, numpy as np; print('OpenCV version:', cv2.__version__)\"","Cwd":"C:\\Users\\win-10\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\neurax_app","WaitMsBeforeAsync":3000,"toolAction":"Checking OpenCV","toolSummary":"Verify cv2 import"}}]}
